        "body": "## Problem\nCodex currently loads user skills from two locations:\n- deprecated: `$CODEX_HOME/skills`\n- current: `~/.agents/skills`\n\nThe second path is hardcoded to the home directory, which makes XDG-managed environments awkward (for example, when users keep agent config under `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/agents`).\n\n## Purpose\nIntroduce an explicit agents-home resolver so user skills can be rooted outside `~` while preserving existing behavior.\n\n## Why this change was created\nUsers who manage config declaratively (Nix/Home Manager, XDG-first setups) need a first-class way to redirect the user skill root. The codebase already has a strong, predictable pattern for this with `CODEX_HOME`, so this PR applies the same pattern to agents home.\n\n## Design Goal: Mirror Existing `CODEX_HOME` Semantics\nThis implementation intentionally **mimics the existing `CODEX_HOME` logic** in `codex-utils-home-dir`:\n- env var is honored when set\n- empty env var is treated as unset\n- set path must exist\n- set path must be a directory\n- set path is canonicalized\n- if unset, a deterministic default path is used\n\nFor agents home, that means:\n- env var: `AGENTS_HOME`\n- default: `~/.agents`\n\nNo implicit `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` fallback is added by design; users can opt in explicitly with:\n`AGENTS_HOME=$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/agents`\n\n## What changed\n### 1) New resolver in shared utility crate\n- Added `find_agents_home()` in `codex-rs/utils/home-dir/src/lib.rs`\n- Added test coverage matching `find_codex_home()` cases:\n  - missing path is fatal\n  - file path is fatal\n  - valid directory canonicalizes\n  - unset env uses default home-based path\n\n### 2) Skills loader now uses resolved agents home\n- Updated user-scope root construction in `codex-rs/core/src/skills/loader.rs` to use:\n  - `$AGENTS_HOME/skills` (defaulting to `~/.agents/skills`)\n- Kept deprecated `$CODEX_HOME/skills` loading unchanged for backward compatibility.\n- If `AGENTS_HOME` is invalid, loader logs a warning and skips that root instead of failing all skill discovery.\n\n### 3) Test determinism improvements in loader tests\n- Added a test helper to avoid ambient host user skills leaking into expectations during unit tests.\n- This keeps `skills::loader` tests deterministic on machines where personal skills already exist.\n\n## Backward compatibility\n- \u2705 Existing users of `~/.agents/skills` are unaffected.\n- \u2705 Existing users of deprecated `$CODEX_HOME/skills` are unaffected.\n- \u2705 New behavior is opt-in via `AGENTS_HOME`.\n\n## How to use with XDG\nExample:\n```bash\nexport AGENTS_HOME=\"$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/agents\"\n```\nCodex will then discover user skills from:\n```text\n$AGENTS_HOME/skills\n```\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt`\n- `cargo test -p codex-utils-home-dir --locked`\n- `nix develop /home/vx/git/codex --command sh -lc 'cd /home/vx/git/codex/codex-rs && GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0 CARGO_NET_GIT_FETCH_WITH_CLI=true cargo test -p codex-core skills::loader'`\n\n## Related issue\n- #1980\n",
